# ######## CELL 10: STAGE = e2e_bipolar  |  estimated run time ~1.5-2.5 h on 8-core High-RAM CPU ########
# ==== HDC on memristive crossbars, v2: 7 datasets, 3 encoders, 6 training rules, ====
# ==== PCM / NeuRRAM ReRAM / CMO-HfOx ReRAM, end-to-end analog, flip-law statistics ====
# e2e_bipolar: end-to-end analog HDC with a +/-1 projection matrix (fix for drift-induced
# encoder bit flips; largemargin, 4bit, 7 datasets, D 512/2048/8192, 3 seeds, 3 devices).
# Runtime: CPU + High-RAM (no GPU needed). Estimated wall time on 8 cores (High-RAM),
# from pilot timings; the log prints a live ETA after each finished job:
#   "core"      main benchmark                       done (10.3 h measured)
#   "encoders"  ID-level encoder                     ~2-2.5 h
#   "e2e"       encoder in the crossbar as well      ~2.5-3.5 h
#   "stress"    device noise x0.5..x8, centring       ~3-4 h
#   "precision" 2-bit cells, ideal periphery          ~1.5-2 h
#   remaining total                                  ~9-12 h (resumable, can span sessions)
# On a 2-core standard runtime multiply by ~4 and expect out-of-memory errors at D=8192.
# Setup (first run in a fresh runtime): ~2 min for the Python 3.12 env + dataset download.
# Results are appended to Google Drive (v2_<stage>.jsonl). If the session drops, run the
# cell again: finished jobs are skipped and the stage continues. The log prints an ETA.
# To split a long stage over several sessions, set DATASETS to a subset, e.g. "mnist".

